  "body": "## Summary\n\nFood amounts could become unreachable when the add-food sheet was shortened, and editing `0.25` to `0.250001` silently kept the old quantity.\n\nThe selected-food sheet now scrolls its controls and editor together. Existing-log edits compare the quantities at the established serving precision, preserving the supported six-decimal change without changing step increments or unit conversion.\n\nCloses #448. No dependency on another open PR.\n\n## Test plan and evidence\n\n- At 390×420, the baseline clips the quantity editor completely. The proposed sheet lets Amount and Add scroll into view and saves the typed `0.125`.\n- Changing `0.25` to `0.250001` now sends `1.000004` servings and reopens with `0.250001` after reload. Both immediate Save and blur-before-Save regressions fail on the baseline and pass here.\n- Ordinary decimals/comma input, invalid and empty values, step precision, conversion/calories, and synthetic offline/lost-acknowledgement replay retain their behavior.\n\n| Before — shortened add-food sheet | After — Amount is reachable |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Before: fixed controls obscure the quantity editor](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/blob/a8bec0320107fae14f8dd53f3aa90571901b6b68/implementation/matched-before-results/capture-short-selected-food-sheet/short.png?raw=true) | ![After: the sheet scrolls to the typed quantity](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/blob/a8bec0320107fae14f8dd53f3aa90571901b6b68/implementation/matched-after-results/capture-short-selected-food-sheet/short.png?raw=true) |\n\n| Before — reopening loses the precise edit | After — reopening preserves it |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Before: reopened amount is 0.25](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/blob/a8bec0320107fae14f8dd53f3aa90571901b6b68/implementation/matched-before-results/capture-supported-precision-after-save-and-reload/reopened.png?raw=true) | ![After: reopened amount is 0.250001](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/blob/a8bec0320107fae14f8dd53f3aa90571901b6b68/implementation/matched-after-results/capture-supported-precision-after-save-and-reload/reopened.png?raw=true) |\n\nMatched synthetic browser captures: base `547206a1b372b73fc95fc412ad453b8099440000` → proposed `ff05e56ed338ec2c178dc05cdf77125d34395c67`. [Builds, fixtures, traces, hashes and preserved scoping originals](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/blob/a8bec0320107fae14f8dd53f3aa90571901b6b68/README.md) are retained outside product history.\n\n## Checks and limits\n\nClient type-check, 56 focused component/utility tests, three maintained browser regressions and 18 additional browser controls pass. Replay uses the real client outbox with a synthetic API; no live database result is claimed. Native-device testing remains deferred. These results address the two demonstrated defects, not an unverified general native-keyboard or fractional-input failure.\n",
